---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import site from '../config/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description={`Terms of use for ${site.domain}, including required Medicare marketing disclosures and the limits of the information published here.`}
  path="/terms/"
  h1="Terms of Use"
  lede="What this website is, what it is not, and the disclosures required of anyone marketing Medicare plans."
  updated="August 2, 2026"
>
  <h2>Required Medicare disclosures</h2>
  <p>
    The CMS third-party marketing organisation disclaimer and our non-affiliation statement appear
    in the footer of <strong>every page on this site</strong>, including this one — scroll down and
    you will find them below. They are deliberately published once per page rather than repeated,
    so there is a single authoritative wording rather than two copies to reconcile.
  </p>
  <p>
    {site.name} is a licensed independent insurance agency. {site.agent.name} is a licensed
    insurance agent, National Producer Number {site.agent.npn}, licensed in
    {' '}{site.agent.statesLicensed} states.
  </p>

  <h2>This site is information, not advice</h2>
  <p>
    Everything published here is general information about Medicare. It is not medical advice, not
    legal advice and not tax advice, and it is not a recommendation of any specific insurance plan
    for any specific person.
  </p>
  <p>
    A recommendation requires knowing your circumstances — your providers, your medications, your
    ZIP code, your finances. That is what a conversation is for, and nothing on this site
    substitutes for one.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy and the passage of time</h2>
  <p>
    Medicare changes every plan year. Premiums, deductibles, coinsurance amounts, income
    thresholds, plan benefits, provider networks and drug formularies are all reset annually, and
    some change mid-year.
  </p>
  <p>
    We label figures with the plan year they apply to and update them when new figures are
    published. Even so, always confirm current details before acting on anything here. If a page
    shows a plan year that has already passed, treat every number on it as historical.
  </p>

  <h2>The free tools</h2>
  <p>
    The calculators and checkers on this site produce <strong>estimates</strong>. They run entirely
    in your browser using the figures you enter and published federal amounts for the stated plan
    year.
  </p>
  <p>They are not quotes, and specifically:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>They do not price any actual insurance plan or name any carrier or product.</li>
    <li>They do not check whether your doctors are in any network.</li>
    <li>They do not price your medications against any plan's formulary.</li>
    <li>
      They do not make Social Security's IRMAA determination — Social Security does that and will
      notify you directly.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Use them to ask better questions. Do not use them as the basis for an enrollment decision on
    their own.
  </p>

  <h2>No cost to you</h2>
  <p>
    There is never a fee to you for our services. Insurance carriers pay commissions to licensed
    agents at rates set by the Centers for Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services. Your premium is
    identical whether you enroll through us, through a call centre, or directly with the carrier.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    We link to Medicare.gov, the Social Security Administration and similar resources for your
    convenience. We do not control those sites and are not responsible for their content. Following
    a link means their terms and privacy policies apply, not ours.
  </p>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The text, design and code of this site are the property of {site.legalName}. You are welcome to
    read it, print it and share links to it. Republishing the content as your own is not permitted.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    This site is provided as-is. To the fullest extent permitted by law, {site.legalName} is not
    liable for any loss arising from reliance on information published here. Your enrollment
    decisions are made with the carrier and with Medicare, and the governing documents are the plan
    documents — not this website.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the State of {site.address.regionName}, without regard
    to conflict-of-law principles.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or call
    <a href={site.phone.href}>{site.phone.display}</a>. For information on all of your Medicare
    options, contact <a href="https://www.medicare.gov" rel="noopener">Medicare.gov</a> or call
    1-800-MEDICARE.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
